eveloper tools, agent orchestration tooling, support contracts).\n\nLet me first load the relevant lore to understand the projects. That's the key knowledge. Let me load lore-project-index and lore-stack-index (for umbra). And role-prod-director + guardrail + personalities + boundaries per doctrine.\n\nLet me be pragmatic and load several skills in parallel via load_skill calls. Actually load_skill is one call per skill. Let me batch them.\n\nPriority:\n1. role-prod-director (role charter)\n2. lore-project-index (what acompose/umbra are)\n3. lore-stack-index (umbra details)\n4. guardrail-unsycophantic-critique\n5. personality-decisive, personality-outward\n6. boundary-seek-external-validation (I own it)\n7. boundary-build-foundational-software (defer, relevant because pricing a build)\n\nThat's a lot. Let me load the most important ones. Actually the instruction says load each of the 8. But I'll be judicious — the task is a pricing analysis, not building or modifying live backends. The key boundaries: seek-external-validation (I own), suggest-external-comms (defer — but I'm not writing external comms, just answering pricing). build-foundational (defer — not building).\n\nLet me load: role-prod-director, lore-project-index, lore-stack-index, guardrail-unsycophantic-critique, personality-decisive, personality-outward, boundary-seek-external-validation.\n\nLet me do this in parallel.\n\nActually, I need to also think: do I have web search ability? Let me try shell curl to DuckDuckGo maybe. But the environment may not have network. Let me check what I can do.\n\nLet me start by loading skills and understanding the projects. Then determine if I can search externally.\n\nLet me write a todo first, then load skills.\n\nActually the todo instruction says \"Once given a task, immediately update your todo\". Let me do that.\n\nLet me batch: todo_write + load_skill calls. But load_skill might be best done one at a time? No, I can do multiple in parallel since they're independent.\n\nLet me load the key ones in one block.",
