    {
      "id": "msg_f6c6f258-403e-4322-86f8-e56d0032d84f",
      "role": "user",
      "created": 1790143925,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "toolResponse",
          "id": "call_00_bfiLlWWoWY3W8M8XuxHu1245",
          "toolResult": {
            "status": "success",
            "value": {
              "resultType": "complete",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Cerbos Hub Pricing | Cerbos\nCerbos Hub Pricing Calculator | Cerbos\nCerbos Pricing 2026: Plans, Hidden Costs &amp; Alternatives\nCerbos Pricing 2026\nCerbos Reviews, Pricing &amp; Alternatives (2026) | Toolradar\nCerbos Software Pricing, Alternatives &amp; More 2026 | Capterra\nCerbos Pricing | Pricing.md\nCerbos 2026 Pricing, Features, Reviews &amp; Alternatives | GetApp\nCerbos Pricing 2026 | SoftwareHope\nCerbos Review 2026: 7.8/10, Free and Open Source\n===SNIPPETS===\nresult__snippet\" href=\"https://www.cerbos.dev/pricing\">Our scalable, open-source authorization layer gives your product secure, decoupled, extensible access controls. Get started with Cerbos today.\nresult__snippet\" href=\"https://www.cerbos.dev/pricing-build-your-plan\">$ 0.25 Per principal $ 25 Per month Start 3 month free trial No credit card required Trusted by hundreds of companies\nresult__snippet\" href=\"https://toolradar.com/tools/cerbos/pricing\">85/100 Cerbos offers a generous free tier and a Proof of Concept plan, making it highly accessible for evaluation and small-scale use. The jump from the free PoC to the $25/month Development tier is reasonable, but the leap to the $933/month Production tier is significant, indicating a strong focus on enterprise-level customers.\nresult__snippet\" href=\"https://www.g2.com/products/cerbos/pricing\">Learn more about the cost of Cerbos, different pricing plans, starting costs, free trials, and more pricing-related information provided by Cerbos.\nresult__snippet\" href=\"https://toolradar.com/tools/cerbos\">Yes, Cerbos can be deployed in various environments, including cloud, self-hosted, on-premise, and air-gapped setups. This ensures flexibility for organizations with strict network security requirements.\nresult__snippet\" href=\"https://www.capterra.com/p/276390/Cerbos/\">Cerbos Open-Source Authorization Layer is an access control system that provides a scalable open-source authorization layer for implementing roles and permissions. The self-hosted software allows developers to decouple and centrally manage authorization logic across applications and services to reduce repetition, gain visibility, and instantly push access changes across systems. Read more\nresult__snippet\" href=\"https://latest.sh/tool/cerbos\">Compare Cerbos pricing tiers, free tier limits, and switching costs. Verified 2026-09-06.\nresult__snippet\" href=\"https://www.getapp.com/security-software/a/cerbos/\">Cerbos PDPs are serverless, stateless, self-hosted services you can run as a sidecar alongside your application. In distributed architectures, Cerbos lets you place a PDP at every microservice and keep all of them up-to-date and synchronized. Cerbos supports authorization across environments—on-premise, cloud, Kubernetes, serverless setups.\nresult__snippet\" href=\"https://app.softwarehope.com/software/cerbos/pricing\">Cerbos pricing guide. Compare 1 plans starting at Contact. Free trial available. Compare verified user reviews, key features, pricing plans, pros and cons...\nresult__snippet\" href=\"https://makerstack.co/reviews/cerbos-review/\">Pricing Cerbos is open source under the Apache 2.0 license. The self-hosted PDP is completely free with no feature restrictions. Cerbos Hub (the managed cloud layer) starts at $99/month and scales based on the number of connected PDPs and policy evaluations. Enterprise plans with SLA guarantees and dedicated support are available on request.",
                  "annotations": {
                    "priority": 0.0
                  }
                }
              ],
              "structuredContent": {
                "stdout": "Cerbos Hub Pricing | Cerbos\nCerbos Hub Pricing Calculator | Cerbos\nCerbos Pricing 2026: Plans, Hidden Costs &amp; Alternatives\nCerbos Pricing 2026\nCerbos Reviews, Pricing &amp; Alternatives (2026) | Toolradar\nCerbos Software Pricing, Alternatives &amp; More 2026 | Capterra\nCerbos Pricing | Pricing.md\nCerbos 2026 Pricing, Features, Reviews &amp; Alternatives | GetApp\nCerbos Pricing 2026 | SoftwareHope\nCerbos Review 2026: 7.8/10, Free and Open Source\n===SNIPPETS===\nresult__snippet\" href=\"https://www.cerbos.dev/pricing\">Our scalable, open-source authorization layer gives your product secure, decoupled, extensible access controls. Get started with Cerbos today.\nresult__snippet\" href=\"https://www.cerbos.dev/pricing-build-your-plan\">$ 0.25 Per principal $ 25 Per month Start 3 month free trial No credit card required Trusted by hundreds of companies\nresult__snippet\" href=\"https://toolradar.com/tools/cerbos/pricing\">85/100 Cerbos offers a generous free tier and a Proof of Concept plan, making it highly accessible for evaluation and small-scale use. The jump from the free PoC to the $25/month Development tier is reasonable, but the leap to the $933/month Production tier is significant, indicating a strong focus on enterprise-level customers.\nresult__snippet\" href=\"https://www.g2.com/products/cerbos/pricing\">Learn more about the cost of Cerbos, different pricing plans, starting costs, free trials, and more pricing-related information provided by Cerbos.\nresult__snippet\" href=\"https://toolradar.com/tools/cerbos\">Yes, Cerbos can be deployed in various environments, including cloud, self-hosted, on-premise, and air-gapped setups. This ensures flexibility for organizations with strict network security requirements.\nresult__snippet\" href=\"https://www.capterra.com/p/276390/Cerbos/\">Cerbos Open-Source Authorization Layer is an access control system that provides a scalable open-source authorization layer for implementing roles and permissions. The self-hosted software allows developers to decouple and centrally manage authorization logic across applications and services to reduce repetition, gain visibility, and instantly push access changes across systems. Read more\nresult__snippet\" href=\"https://latest.sh/tool/cerbos\">Compare Cerbos pricing tiers, free tier limits, and switching costs. Verified 2026-09-06.\nresult__snippet\" href=\"https://www.getapp.com/security-software/a/cerbos/\">Cerbos PDPs are serverless, stateless, self-hosted services you can run as a sidecar alongside your application. In distributed architectures, Cerbos lets you place a PDP at every microservice and keep all of them up-to-date and synchronized. Cerbos supports authorization across environments—on-premise, cloud, Kubernetes, serverless setups.\nresult__snippet\" href=\"https://app.softwarehope.com/software/cerbos/pricing\">Cerbos pricing guide. Compare 1 plans starting at Contact. Free trial available. Compare verified user reviews, key features, pricing plans, pros and cons...\nresult__snippet\" href=\"https://makerstack.co/reviews/cerbos-review/\">Pricing Cerbos is open source under the Apache 2.0 license. The self-hosted PDP is completely free with no feature restrictions. Cerbos Hub (the managed cloud layer) starts at $99/month and scales based on the number of connected PDPs and policy evaluations. Enterprise plans with SLA guarantees and dedicated support are available on request.",
                "stderr": "",
                "exit_code": 0
              },
              "isError": false
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "userVisible": true,
        "agentVisible": true
      }
    },
