          "type": "thinking",
          "thinking": "Good, I now have some external pricing references:\n\nCerbos (closest comparable to umbra's policy/authorization half — decoupled policy, self-hosted):\n- Self-hosted PDP is free (Apache 2.0).\n- Cerbos Hub (managed cloud) starts $99/month, scales by PDPs/policy evals. Enterprise with SLA + dedicated support on request.\n- Cerbos Hub pricing: $0.25/principal, $25/month dev tier, $933/month production tier.\n\nDeveloper/DevOps retainers:\n- Freelance developer retainer: 15-40 hrs/month; maintenance/support 10-15 hrs; active dev 20-30 hrs.\n- DevTools marketing retainers $1,250-$7,000/month (not relevant, marketing).\n- Sysadmin/reddit: fixed retainer with scope agreement, discounted prepaid block of hours.\n\nNow I want one more data point: what a \"custom build\" of this kind costs. Actually the more relevant comparison for \"custom one-time cut\" of a dev tool / integration is: senior platform engineer contract rate. I have general knowledge: $150-250/hr US senior platform/DevOps contract. A scoped custom cut (integrate umbra guardfile into a CLI, or wire acompose bundle for a team) might be a 2-6 week engagement.\n\nBut I should be careful: the lore explicitly says the market is commodity for both halves. And the comp rule says don't invent comp numbers — that's about Kai's comp, not product pricing. But I should be honest and mark inferences.\n\nLet me also check one more external: what do people pay for \"MCP gateway\" or agent tool policy — Kong AI Gateway pricing, Permit.io. Actually I have enough. The key external grounding:\n\n1. Cerbos self-hosted = free; Hub from $99/month, prod $933/month. This is the closest analogue to umbra's \"occlusion/policy\" and shows the ceiling: even a funded vendor charges ~$1k/month for production policy, and gives the engine away free.\n\n2. Freelance retainer: 10-40 hrs/month.\n\nLet me get one more: a \"custom one-time\" price for senior platform contract. Let me search quickly for senior platform engineer contract hourly rate 2026. Actually, I should be efficient. I have enough for a grounded answer. But the guardrail/outward wants me to check the \"would anyone buy\" claim against outside.\n\nActually the most decisive external fact is already in lore: 2026-09-10 category count found both halves commodity, with named OSS competitors and their star counts. That's the \"would anyone buy one\" answer's foundation. Combined with Cerbos pricing ($99-$933/mo for a real funded vendor's policy product, self-hosted free), I can now give honest price bands.\n\nLet me do one more quick search: senior platform engineer / devops contract hourly rate, to ground the \"one-time cut\" price.",
